# 必考词 Unit25
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-必考词
# 描述: 必考词Unit25核心高频词汇

{{aptitude}}{/ˈæptɪtjuːd/}}{n. 天资；才能}}{{She showed a natural aptitude for mathematics at an early age.}}

{{arbitrary}}{/ˈɑːrbɪtreri/}}{adj. 任意的；武断的}}{{The decision seemed arbitrary and unfair to many people.}}

{{array}}{/əˈreɪ/}}{n. 一系列；数组}}{{The store offers a wide array of products to choose from.}}

{{articulate}}{/ɑːˈtɪkjuleɪt/}}{adj. 善于表达的；v. 清楚表达}}{{She is very articulate and can explain complex ideas clearly.}}

{{aspire}}{/əˈspaɪər/}}{v. 渴望；追求}}{{She aspires to become a leading researcher in her field.}}

{{authentic}}{/ɔːˈθentɪk/}}{adj. 真正的；可靠的}}{{The museum displays authentic artifacts from ancient Rome.}}

{{authorize}}{/ˈɔːθəraɪz/}}{v. 授权；批准}}{{Only the manager can authorize large expenditures.}}

{{autonomous}}{/ɔːˈtɒnəməs/}}{adj. 自治的；自主的}}{{The region gained autonomous status after the peace agreement.}}

{{avert}}{/əˈvɜːrt/}}{v. 避免；转移}}{{Quick action by the pilot averted a potential disaster.}}

{{backbone}}{/ˈbækbəʊn/}}{n. 脊梁；支柱}}{{Small businesses are the backbone of the economy.}}

{{bail}}{/beɪl/}}{n. 保释；v. 舀水}}{{The suspect was released on bail pending trial.}}

{{bankrupt}}{/ˈbæŋkrʌpt/}}{adj. 破产的；v. 使破产}}{{The company went bankrupt after years of declining sales.}}

{{barrier}}{/ˈbæriər/}}{n. 障碍；屏障}}{{Lack of education is a barrier to economic development.}}

{{benchmark}}{/ˈbentʃmɑːrk/}}{n. 基准；标准}}{{The test results serve as a benchmark for future assessments.}}

{{bizarre}}{/bɪˈzɑːr/}}{adj. 奇异的；怪诞的}}{{The story had a bizarre twist that surprised everyone.}}

{{bloom}}{/bluːm/}}{v. 开花；n. 花期}}{{The flowers bloom in spring, painting the garden in color.}}

{{bolster}}{/ˈbəʊlstər/}}{v. 支持；加强}}{{The new evidence bolstered the prosecution's case.}}

{{boom}}{/buːm/}}{n. 繁荣；v. 迅速发展}}{{The housing boom led to a surge in construction activity.}}

{{brace}}{/breɪs/}}{v. 准备；n. 支架}}{{The residents braced themselves for the approaching hurricane.}}

{{breach}}{/briːtʃ/}}{n. 违反；v. 突破}}{{The hacker exploited a security breach in the system.}}

{{bureaucracy}}{/bjʊˈrɒkrəsi/}}{n. 官僚机构；官僚主义}}{{Excessive bureaucracy slows down the decision-making process.}}

{{calibrate}}{/ˈkælɪbreɪt/}}{v. 校准；调整}}{{The instrument needs to be calibrated before use.}}

{{camouflage}}{/ˈkæməflɑːʒ/}}{n. 伪装；v. 掩饰}}{{The chameleon uses camouflage to blend in with its surroundings.}}

{{catastrophe}}{/kəˈtæstrəfi/}}{n. 大灾难；浩劫}}{{The earthquake was a catastrophe that affected millions of people.}}

{{chronic}}{/ˈkrɒnɪk/}}{adj. 慢性的；长期的}}{{Chronic stress can lead to serious health problems.}}

{{circulate}}{/ˈsɜːrkjəleɪt/}}{v. 循环；流通}}{{The rumor circulated quickly through the office.}}

{{coexist}}{/ˌkəʊɪɡˈzɪst/}}{v. 共存；和平共处}}{{Different cultures can coexist in a diverse society.}}

{{coherent}}{/kəʊˈhɪərənt/}}{adj. 连贯的；一致的}}{{The essay presents a coherent argument supported by evidence.}}

{{coincide}}{/ˌkəʊɪnˈsaɪd/}}{v. 同时发生；一致}}{{My vacation coincides with the school holidays.}}

{{collaborate}}{/kəˈlæbəreɪt/}}{v. 合作；协作}}{{The two universities collaborate on research projects.}}

{{commemorate}}{/kəˈmeməreɪt/}}{v. 纪念；庆祝}}{{The monument commemorates those who died in the war.}}

{{commence}}{/kəˈmens/}}{v. 开始；着手}}{{The ceremony will commence at 10 a.m. sharp.}}

{{compact}}{/kəmˈpækt/}}{adj. 紧凑的；v. 压缩}}{{The apartment is small but compact and well-designed.}}

{{comparable}}{/ˈkɒmpərəbl/}}{adj. 可比较的；类似的}}{{The quality is comparable to that of more expensive brands.}}

{{compassion}}{/kəmˈpæʃn/}}{n. 同情；怜悯}}{{She showed great compassion for the victims of the disaster.}}

{{compile}}{/kəmˈpaɪl/}}{v. 编辑；汇编}}{{The team compiled a comprehensive report on the findings.}}

{{complementary}}{/ˌkɒmplɪˈmentri/}}{adj. 互补的；补充的}}{{The two approaches are complementary rather than contradictory.}}

{{comply}}{/kəmˈplaɪ/}}{v. 遵守；服从}}{{All businesses must comply with health and safety regulations.}}

{{comprise}}{/kəmˈpraɪz/}}{v. 包含；由...组成}}{{The United Kingdom comprises England, Scotland, Wales, and Northern Ireland.}}

{{conceive}}{/kənˈsiːv/}}{v. 构想；怀孕}}{{It is hard to conceive of a world without technology.}}
